	quests: [
		{
			title: "Lands of Taste and Scent"
			x: -2.5d
			y: 1.0d
			shape: "pentagon"
			description: [
				"&5Looks like the next stops on this journey are the worlds branching from Precasia."
				""
				"&dHm I don't quite remember which world types those were. No wait, wasn't one of them a floral dimension?"
				""
				"&5Garden worlds they call it, yeah. The other one is usually a world made of food in some way."
				""
				"&dOh yeah. That gummy world they had when we last looked into their game server was really...fun looking. And tasty looking."
				""
				"&5Hopefully this time we'll have better luck stopping them. So, Bandit, your next two stops are called Candyland and Gardencia. Both appropriate names for the worlds, I must say."
			]
			dependencies: ["516AD1604BBD2E1D"]
			id: "24052A5E15772F3E"
			tasks: [{
				id: "08FCC5848975C5A3"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "To the Sweet Tasting Land"
			x: 0.0d
			y: -1.5d
			shape: "diamond"
			description: [
				"&5Candyland, as mentioned, is the dimension reserved for food based worlds."
				""
				"&dSpecifically, where the FOP places worlds that are made OUT of food. Not just contains it, but the trees, the plants, the ores, etc."
				""
				"&5Though for player protection, The FOP have disabled consumption of a lot of these materials. Plays havoc with their consumption system it seems."
				""
				"&dBut either way, you can get to Candyland by finding and growing some Heart Fruit in Precasia. You can rarely find the seeds when you break Tangle Thorns. Then just grow em and eat one while in Precasia, with a Blank Realmstone in your inventory."
				""
				"&5Wait, before you enter the Portal, Bandit, you're going to need the Green Dimension DLC! And the Blue Ore DLC, probably. Wait, does Candyland even HAVE ore?"
			]
			dependencies: ["24052A5E15772F3E"]
